# Potassium · K · gate 19

**Potassium** (K) is element **19** of the periodic table — a **alkali metal**, period 4, group 1, s-block, solid at standard conditions, atomic weight **39.098**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Symbol K, from kalium; softer and more violent than sodium; the other half of the nerve impulse.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
Under David Wise's four-state cycle, gate **19** falls on **0:0 = 1 = 0** because (Z−1) mod 4 = **2**. That state is *the collapse where nothing equals one equals nothing — the return to the single source* — the nature of emergence here is **spiritual**. Potassium is not a thing apart; it is the one stochastic element, caught at this beat of its cycle.

## Emergence — spiritual
This emergent carries the **spiritual** nature: the same four — natural · ethereal · spiritual · electrical — that run through every sphere of UD0. Its color is `#e6a849`.

